WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.470
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.380
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.130
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.830
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.930
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.300
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.230
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.480
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:56.750
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:03.490
What is truly precious?

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:12.980
Desperate Situation!
Shadow of Eyes

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.560
It's the morning of the final matches!

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.900
Grandpa...

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.270
Yes?

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.340
Hey!

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.240
Good morning.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.100
Good morning everybody.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.980
It's finally time, Yugi.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.490
Let's go to the location of our final battles.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.280
Yeah.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.600
Let's go!

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:02.370
Yugi and Jonouchi, we'll cheer for you from the terrace.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:05.600
Yugi and Jonouchi, good luck.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:07.940
Yeah.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.450
Good morning, kids.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.460
Yugi, it's now time that we settle things.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.500
Jonouchi, thanks for coming so that I can defeat you.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:41.070
Keith, you may be a former U.S. champion, but I'll crush a cheater like you with my cards!

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:48.600
You still haven't realized that I stole the card you need to enter the tournament.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.880
You've lost even before setting foot in the Duel Ring.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.390
To the duelists participating in the final tournament, thank you for your patience.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.890
Please proceed to the dueling area.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.320
Pegasus!

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:33.220
Honored duelists, welcome to the sacred battlefield.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:40.860
I hereby declare the start of the Duelist Kingdom Championship Tournament!

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:46.870
The winner of the tournament will receive a large monetary prize.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.710
If I get the prize money, I can use it to save Shizuka.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:57.150
And the winner will also earn the right to challenge me.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.720
I have a question for you, Pegasus!

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:03.650
If we defeat you, what do we get?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:13.660
If you defeat the creator of Duel Monsters, Industrial Illusions will recognize you as the first Duelist King.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:19.900
Everyone will acknowledge that you are the #1 duelist in the world.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.740
Everyone will acknowledge...

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.020
#1 in the world.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:31.860
Every duelist here wants the title more than the prize money.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.350
Am I wrong?

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.140
How interesting.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:37.850
I'm gonna win!

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:45.360
I wonder which one of you will win the final tournament and challenge me.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.220
Pegasus!

00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:00.040
I promise to defeat you and free everyone's souls!

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.780
The first match will now begin.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.620
Yugi Muto vs Mai Kujaku.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.220
Proceed to the Duel Ring.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:22.530
Before the duel begins, show me your entry cards.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.200
Good.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.940
Do your best, Yugi!

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.550
Hey you!

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.360
Jonouchi!

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.250
It's a clearer view from here.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.990
Yugi, you better win!

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:51.460
Mai Kujaku, this duel is only a step in defeating Pegasus.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:59.250
The more powerful the duelist, the more joy I feel when I defeat him.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.470
That's why I came to this island.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:05.540
But then I met you.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:11.180
I always relied on my own, but you taught me the warmth of friendship.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:16.420
It became my dream to battle you someday.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.820
Yugi, you changed my life.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:27.120
But you're looking right past me.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:31.820
Your heart is caught up in battling Pegasus.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:36.170
Looking at it another way, it means you're impatient and irritated.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:40.840
Dueling isn't so simple that you can take your eyes off your opponent and win!

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.710
Here I go, Yugi!

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:45.650
Yeah!

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.020
Duel!

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.910
What's wrong, Mai?

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.890
Aren't you going to use your aroma tactics?

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.730
That won't work on you anymore.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:02.570
Sorry Mai, but you're not good enough to defeat me.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.960
You're overlooking something right now.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:09.870
And if you can't see it, there's no way you can defeat me!

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.410
Harpie Lady in attack position!

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:19.130
Mai is using her signature strategy.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.130
Be careful, Yugi!

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.420
Don't worry.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.000
Mai's strategy only has one pattern.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.420
Does she think the same tricks she used on me will work against Yugi?

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:31.790
I'll play another card this turn.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.070
She set a card.

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:42.870
I'll use my main card to destroy Harpie Lady instantly.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:46.010
Gaia The Fierce Knight!

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.010
Attack Harpie Lady!

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.250
You fool.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:55.950
I activate the trap card Mirror Wall!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.150
Spiral Shaver!

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:03.890
What?

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:09.400
The trap card Mirror Wall cuts your monster's attack points in half.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:15.400
When you declare an attack, a mirror wall appears before your monster.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:22.140
The monster attacks its own reflection, cutting its attack points in half.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:25.150
My turn.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.150
It's an Equip Card for Harpie Lady.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.160
Cyber Shield!

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.790
Go, Harpie Lady!

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:39.760
Scratch Crush!

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.000
Gaia The Fierce Knight is destroyed.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:50.510
Impossible!  She destroyed Gaia, my main card?

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:55.260
Yugi, I can't believe you fell for my trap.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.080
I must have overestimated you.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.120
It's your turn, Yugi.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:05.620
Good.  Summoned Skull.

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:09.290
Its attack points can easily destroy Harpie Lady.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:13.300
Attack me, Yugi.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:16.100
I set one card.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.630
I'll battle using this card!

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.440
I'll use power to make you surrender, Mai!

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:30.140
Go, Summoned Skull!  Annihilate Harpie Lady!

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:31.920
Magic Lightning!

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:36.580
Yugi, you declared an attack.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.890
My trap activates again!

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.290
What?

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:49.760
Summoned Skull also loses half its attack points.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.200
I see!  It's a Continuous Trap!

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:56.880
Exactly.  My trap remains on the field.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.110
You realized that a bit too late, Yugi.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:07.400
Normal Trap Cards lose their power after they activate, and they leave the field.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.280
But there are exceptions.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:17.240
Yes.  Out of hundreds of trap cards, Continuous Trap Cards are the rarest, and Mirror Wall is one of them.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:24.800
As long as this card is on the field, it keeps using its effect every time you declare an attack.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:30.910
Yugi, it's the same as if your monsters can no longer attack.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.740
What's wrong with Yugi?

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.740
He's playing too quickly, so his attacks are too simple.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:40.050
It's not like him to fall for the same trick twice!

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.380
Yugi, what's wrong?

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:11.950
I'm disappointed that your dueling skills are not as good as I hoped they'd be.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:20.690
The moment you stepped into the Duel Ring, I could see that unseen pressure was crushing you.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.890
Unseen pressure?

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:28.000
When two duelists face off, they can sense each other's battle aura.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.630
But you currently don't have that aura.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.630
You can't sense my fighting spirit?

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:39.640
That's right!  You're only thinking about battling Pegasus!

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:42.330
You're underestimating me.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.610
You're so conceited.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.320
You thought you defeated me even before the duel began.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:53.020
You're so focused on Pegasus that you're failing in our duel.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.890
Pressure from Pegasus?

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.860
Yugi boy, the lady is right.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:07.060
In your current mental state, you cannot defeat me.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:13.270
Mai, save your lecture until you defeat me!

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:15.210
Continue the duel!

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:21.950
When a weakling takes a hit, he resorts to intimidation to hide his own weakness.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.440
That's enough!

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:24.950
Seems I struck a nerve.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:29.080
That's why you easily fell for my trap twice.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.620
Mai is talking more trash than usual.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.930
Yugi, don't let Mai provoke you!

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:41.320
Mai, you don't have to be so cruel.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:46.310
Wait...  Is Mai provoking Yugi on purpose?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:51.180
Win or lose.  The result is all that matters in competition.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:54.880
In the end, you can only count on yourself!

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:58.930
Mai is always hard on herself.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:02.620
So she can't forgive Yugi for not using his true strength.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:06.730
You've angered me, Mai!

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:10.660
Have you come to your senses, Yugi?

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:13.300
Maybe we can now have a proper duel.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:14.900
Here I go!

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.540
The real battle now begins!

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.940
Yeah!  I'll take whatever you got!

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.600
Good, Yugi.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:26.180
As a duelist, you must use 100% of your power and risk your pride.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:28.920
Or there's no point in defeating you.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.920
Should my Harpie attack his Summoned Skull this turn?

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:40.060
His set card worries me.  It may be a trap.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:41.530
In that case...

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:44.800
I won't attack this turn, but I'll play this card.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.570
Harpie's Feather Duster!

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.330
My set card was Spellbinding Circle.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:08.060
If you attacked, my trap card would've caught you.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:09.820
That was good anticipation, Mai.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.660
I'm a careful person.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.530
You should follow my example.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.660
It's your turn, Yugi.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:23.240
As long as she has Mirror Wall, my monsters will lose attack points if they attack.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:26.020
She's prevented me from attacking.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.210
I switch Summoned Skull to defense position.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.180
I place another monster in defense position.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.900
Since you can't attack, there's no way you can win.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:44.120
It's my turn!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.560
I use the Equip Card Rose Whip to raise Harpie Lady's attack points!

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:58.140
You're going to keep powering up Harpie Lady while hiding behind Mirror Wall?

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:00.740
First, I'll attack your defending monster!

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.080
Whip Punish!

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.400
I'm not done, Yugi.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.180
I still haven't completed my Harpie combo.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.080
Hey, is Yugi going to be okay?

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:19.000
Yugi, Mai will try to multiply her Harpie Lady!  Be careful!

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.730
Do your best, Yugi!

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.730
I play a monster in defense position!

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.900
If I don't get rid of Mai's trap card, I'm going to lose!

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.200
It's no use defending.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:31.200
I'll cook you up nicely.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:33.880
My turn!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:35.730
It's here!

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:40.020
With this card, my Harpie combo is 70% complete.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:43.780
It's not perfect, but it's good enough to defeat you.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.800
Here I go, Yugi!

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:48.460
This is the Harpie's most powerful servant!

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.280
What's that?

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.600
Harpie's Pet Dragon!

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.570
It's Harpie Lady's obedient and cute pet.

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:06.570
Harpie's Pet Dragon gains 300 attack points for every Harpie on the field.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:09.310
Destroy Summoned Skull!

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:12.500
Saint Fire Giga!

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.520
Even my Summoned Skull?

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:23.680
Yugi, you're forgetting something important.

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:24.320
What?

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:29.560
Unless you find the answer, there's no way you can defeat me.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:34.260
When I previously dueled Jonouchi, I was asked a question.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:39.310
I'll now ask you the same question.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:42.310
What can be seen but remains unseen?

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.880
Yugi, do you know the answer?

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:48.380
Seen but remains unseen?

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:52.520
Mai, that's the same question I asked you!

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:55.420
Do you even know the answer?

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:57.760
Yes, Jonouchi.

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:00.860
I found my own answer to your question.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:05.120
Then I'll answer for Yugi.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:10.680
The answer is strong friendship!  How's that!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.640
You idiot!  That's the wrong answer!

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.640
The answer isn't so cheap.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.520
Cheap?

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.380
Then what's the correct answer?

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:23.250
Yugi and I are the ones who created that riddle!

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:29.820
What are you doing?

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.280
Jonouchi, you taught me the answer.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.830
You should know the answer yourself.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:43.840
How could an amateur like you win your way through the Duelist Kingdom?

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:45.960
The answer lies there.

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:50.510
But Yugi isn't currently capable of answering this question.

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:56.240
I can't let Mai's words confuse me right now.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:59.250
I will win this duel with my own strength!

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.820
Good.  My card is Dark Magician.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:08.100
Harpie's Pet Dragon has 2300 attack points.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.260
My Dark Magician has more attack points.

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:17.270
But I can't attack because she has the Continuous Trap Mirror Wall.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:19.400
Then I'll fight her trap with a trap.

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:25.510
I set one card and play Dark Magician in defense position.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:29.100
I end my turn.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:36.940
Mai, if you attack my Dark Magician, Mirror Force will destroy all your monsters.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:38.390
It's my turn.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.530
With this card, my Harpie combo is 80% complete.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:49.530
Yugi, your traps won't work against me.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.940
My card is the Equip Card Shadow of Eyes!

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:55.770
Shadow of Eyes?

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:59.340
Look at the Duel Ring to learn about this card's effect.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:02.530
What?

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.120
Dark Magician is in attack position!

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:06.730
That's right.

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:09.650
Shadow of Eyes tempts your monster to fight!

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:14.660
My Harpie's battle pheromones stimulate the enemy's fighting instincts!

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.880
She's forcing him to attack?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.500
That means Yugi can't defend anymore either.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:27.710
Now Dark Magician, attack my Harpie!

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:40.720
I'll also play this card.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.620
Harpie's Feather Duster.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:51.200
My trap card!

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:54.130
Harpie's Pet Dragon attacks!

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.130
Saint Fire Giga!

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.330
Well, Yugi?

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:09.210
Isn't my Harpie combo perfect?

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.460
Yugi is in trouble!

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:12.220
Yugi...

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.260
What can be seen but remains unseen?

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:42.330
Mai's words bring Yugi back to himself, allowing him to counterattack.

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:48.530
But Mai's overwhelming strategy puts him on the verge of defeat again!

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:53.130
What?  You have a trump card to turn this situation around?

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:57.600
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
The Legendary Strongest Warrior
Black Luster Soldier Descends

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.960
Duel, standby!

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:12.390
The flask glistens

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:20.230
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:29.210
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:36.980
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:42.820
Shower of happiness

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.930
I will shower you with it

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:55.200
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:59.440
Shower of happiness

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:03.570
You are not alone

